  "phase3_gemini_self_healing": {
    "forensics": "Three of the five losses (INFY, ITC, TATASTEEL morning) experienced exact 0.65% stop-loss whipsaws during the 09:45-10:25 AM transition period, where initial retail liquidity sweeps lacked sufficient institutional continuation volume at the 2.15x threshold. The remaining two losses (TATASTEEL afternoon, ICICIBANK) were entered after 13:45 IST and stagnated into EOD square-off, where low afternoon volatility failed to reach the ambitious 1.45% target and statutory brokerage fees eroded marginal gross gains into net losses.",
    "learning": "In NSE large-cap cash equities, overcoming high retail fee drag (~84% of gross profit in Cycle #29) requires higher volume conviction on liquidity sweeps to filter morning bull traps, paired with a tighter breakeven trigger and realistic profit targets that capture intraday momentum before afternoon consolidation.",
