    "plan_update_summary": "### Cycle #29 Review & Cycle #30 Mutation\nOut-of-sample testing with DeepSeek V4.1 Flash achieved net profitability (\u20b9+7.06, PF: 1.09, 50% WR), outperforming the 1-year baseline, but suffered heavily from statutory fee drag (\u20b937.10 fees vs \u20b944.16 gross profit). Forensic analysis of the losing cluster revealed two structural vulnerabilities: morning entries (09:45\u201310:25 IST) getting clipped by standard 0.65% stops due to false breakouts, and late-afternoon entries (post-13:45 IST) stalling into EOD square-off where transaction costs turned flat/positive gross trades into net losses. For Cycle #30, we are increasing `min_sweep_vol_multiplier` to 2.35x and widening `min_sl_pct` to 0.70% to absorb morning institutional stop-hunting noise. Concurrently, we are tightening `breakeven_trigger_r` to 0.85R and calibrating `min_target_pct` to 1.35% to lock in defensive exits against fee erosion and improve target hit rates before the EOD liquidity taper."
